& [JustificationRecord: ChatWorkbenchKeyboardAffordances: 2026-05-14] is the justification for keyboard-accessible refinement controls
  + [justification_uuid] is 905915c4-3603-4ab4-8806-8c455922800f
  + [work_uuid] is 4689f62b-a60f-409e-9f57-978b089691c4
  + [specification_anchor] is [ImplementationFrontier: ChatRefinementV2] frontier_5
  + [requirement] is add accessible keyboard equivalents for select, insert, remove, reveal source, and toggle frames
  + [fork_commit] is 5d67cfaa
  + [solution] is Chat, Cutting, and Editing toggles now expose explicit show/hide aria labels
  + [solution] is the source staging arrow now exposes an aria label
  + [solution] is the insertion bridge arrow now exposes an insert aria label
  + [solution] is insertion position can be moved through up/down bridge step buttons without pointer drag
  + [solution] is remove and reveal-source controls now expose target-specific aria labels
  + [data_design_reason] is insertion_position remains an explicit interaction state that can be changed without pointer-only control flow
  + [ui_interaction_reason] is every core raw-to-cut-to-edit operation has a keyboard-addressable control path

  = must: preserve pointer drag as an expert shortcut while keeping keyboard operation available
  = must: keep disabled keyboard controls visibly blocked when the transition guard fails
  = should: add deeper browser-level accessibility checks when automation becomes available

